
Linux important Commands :::


Find out the top most big directories - 
===========================

du -sch *|grep G | tail 

du -hsx * | sort -rh | head -10

sudo du -ah /var/log | sort -rh | head -n 10

Sometimes the above command errors  -> bash: /usr/bin/du: Argument list too long , so below command can be of use

find . -maxdepth 1 ! -name "." -exec du -hsx {} + | sort -rh | head -10



Example command to find these files by timestamp:
find /u02/app/oracle/diag/rdbms/usanopxq_iadad3/usanopxq5/trace/ -name "*.trc"  -newermt "2024-07-05 04:25:00" -not -newermt "2024-07-05 05:50:00"

Find files for last n days : 
find . -mtime -2


Remove files :
find . -type f -name "*.log" -exec rm {} \;


Top CPU/Mem consuming process : 
ps -eo pid,ppid,cmd,%mem,%cpu --sort=-%cpu | head


To see memory for specific set of process:
ps -aux | head -n 1; ps -aux | egrep 'ora_p0|ora_pp' | sort -k6,6 -g -r | head



Kill all the process related to foreground process oracle :
ps -ef |grep ora_p[0-9]*|grep -v grep|awk '{print  $2}'|xargs kill -9




ACFS Check for corruption : 
/usr/local/bin/dcli -l opc -g ~/dbs_group "sudo bash -c "/sbin/acfsutil info fs /acfs01""|grep -i corrupt


Image info checking post patch using opc  :
/usr/local/bin/dcli -g /tmp/olsnodes.txt -l opc 'sudo /usr/local/bin/imageinfo -version'


EXTRACT THE NO OF THE INDIVIDUAL ORA ERRORS REPORTED IN DB ALERT LOG :-
grep -Eo 'ORA-[0-9]{5}' alert*.log | sort | uniq -c | sort -nr



